@startuml sd_forwarding_get_route
title Scenario: GET a route held by another replica, with one replica down

autonumber
actor "ATCC" as c
participant "Entry (Envoy)" as e
participant "airports-routes-0" as r0
participant "airports-routes-1" as r1
participant "airports-routes-2" as r2

c -> e : GET /api/routes/OPO/LIS (JWT)
e -> r0 : GET /api/routes/OPO/LIS
r0 -> r0 : look up locally: not found\n(RouteNotFoundException)
note right of r0
  PeerForwardingAdvice: not forwarded yet
  (no X-Peer-Forwarded), so ask every peer
  in parallel (PeerClient)
end note
par
  r0 -> r1 : GET /api/routes/OPO/LIS\nX-Peer-Forwarded, JWT, X-Correlation-Id
  r1 -> r1 : look up locally: found
  r1 --> r0 : 200 + route (ETag)
else
  r0 -> r2 : GET /api/routes/OPO/LIS\nX-Peer-Forwarded, JWT, X-Correlation-Id
  r2 -x r0 : no answer (connect 0.5 s, read 2 s,\n1 retry, then circuit breaker)
end
r0 --> e : 200 + route, X-Data-Node: airports-routes-1
e --> c : 200 + route

== Alternatives ==
note over r0
  Every peer answers 404                   -> 404
  No peer has it, but some did not answer  -> 503, Retry-After: 1,
                                              X-Partial-Result: true, X-Unreachable-Peers
  A forwarded request (X-Peer-Forwarded) is never forwarded again (no loops).
end note
@enduml
